GroupLab {version}
==================

GroupLab measures how accurately a rifle shoots, and tells you how much its
figures can be trusted. This is a test build for Windows. It is not finished
software: see "What is not done yet" below.

Built from https://github.com/oRAirwolf/grouplab at commit {commit}, on {date}.


RUNNING IT
----------

1. Unzip this folder anywhere you like. Your Downloads folder is fine.
2. Double-click GroupLab.App.exe.

Windows will probably say "Windows protected your PC". That is SmartScreen,
and it says that about any program nobody has paid to sign. Click "More info",
then "Run anyway". GroupLab is unsigned because signing costs money the
project has not spent. The source of this exact build is public at the commit
above, so you can read every line of it if you want to.

Your antivirus may also quarantine it, for the same reason: it is an unsigned
program that unpacks a lot of files. If it does, the file it took is
GroupLab.App.exe.


TRY IT WITHOUT A RIFLE
----------------------

The samples folder has two sheets you can open straight away.

- samples/gl-cf25-ltr-d-25-shots-600-dpi.png is a real GroupLab sheet, shot at
  100 yards with 25 rounds, one at each bull, and scanned at 600 dpi. Open it
  and GroupLab reads the sheet's printed codes, registers the page, finds the
  holes, and gives you the figures. samples/PROVENANCE.md says whose sheet it
  is and what was agreed before it was published.

    In GroupLab: the menu at the top right, "Open image", then that file.
    Then press "Accept and analyse".

- samples/gl-cf25-ltr-300-dpi.png is a real 300 dpi scan of an unshot sheet,
  printed on Alan's own printer. It shows what registration does on paper that
  has been through a printer and a scanner.

The sample with shots is generated by GroupLab itself, so it carries nobody's
data. It is not a photograph of a real target.


PRINTING A SHEET
----------------

The Print screen prints any of the twenty built-in sheets at actual size.
Print through "Open to print" today, and print at Actual size or 100 percent,
never Fit to page. Measure bull 1 to bull 5 with a ruler before you shoot it:
on the Letter 5x5 sheet that distance is 5.98 in (152.0 mm).


WHERE GROUPLAB PUTS THINGS
--------------------------

Everything it keeps is in one folder, under your own user account:

    %APPDATA%\GroupLab

That folder holds settings.json, grouplab.db (your sessions and records),
sheets (any sheet you design), and the log. GroupLab writes nothing else
anywhere, and it sends nothing anywhere: there is no account, no telephoning
home, and no network use at all.

To remove GroupLab: delete the folder you unzipped, and delete
%APPDATA%\GroupLab. That is all of it. If you used the installer, use
"Add or remove programs" instead, and it will leave %APPDATA%\GroupLab alone
so your sessions survive; delete that folder yourself when you want it gone.


WHEN SOMETHING IS WRONG
-----------------------

The gear at the bottom left opens the settings, and "Report a problem" there
makes a report package: a zip with the log and what GroupLab was doing. It
carries no location data and no images unless you add them. Send it to Alan
with a line about what you were doing.


WHAT IS NOT DONE YET
--------------------

This is an honest list, and the README in the repository is the authority.

- Printing from inside GroupLab (the "Print" button) lost every marker and
  code on one printer. That is fixed, but no sheet from the fixed version has
  been checked on paper yet, so use "Open to print" for now.
- Hole detection on blank paper, with no sheet definition, is not built.
- Garmin Xero import is not built; chronograph readings are typed in.
- Linux and macOS builds exist and are tested, but nobody has used them.
- Several of the project's own gates have no material yet, so the figures
  should be read as a careful piece of software that has not been proved on
  a large body of real targets.


